{% set local_problem %}
<p>Here's an uncomfortable truth about Hampton Cove homes: even on houses that sell for half a million dollars or more, builders typically install the cheapest gutters that meet code. It's not malicious — it's economics. Gutters don't sell houses, so builders minimize that line item.</p>

<p>The result is homes with stunning kitchens, beautiful landscaping, and gutters that belong on a starter home. Thin-gauge aluminum. Seams every 10 feet. Undersized for North Alabama's rainfall. These systems look fine initially, but after 5-10 years they start failing — leaking at seams, overflowing during moderate rain, pulling away from fascia boards.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters solve this mismatch. Heavy-gauge materials that won't dent or corrode. No seams to leak. Custom fabrication for even complex Hampton Cove rooflines. Finally, gutters that match the quality of the home they're attached to.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. We fabricate them on-site using portable equipment, cutting each run to the exact length needed for your roofline.</p>

<p>This matters because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter is a potential leak point and a place for debris to accumulate. Seamless construction eliminates these weak points entirely. The result is better performance, cleaner aesthetics, and dramatically longer lifespan.</p>
{% endset %}

